Releasing version mvm04a.  Added a new command, #stance, to control
whether the character takes an aggressive, or defensive, posture in
fighting and general demeanor.

http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/patches.shtml#mvm

DETAILS SPOILER:

Void and #stance are calculated for all roles, but affect only monks.

#stance sets whether the player postures aggressively or defensively.
For monks, the void modifier is split between to-hit and to-be-hit
depending on the stance.  An aggressive monk will add any positive
void modifier to to-hit, but shift any negative void modifier to
to-be-hit (eg, AC).  A defensive monk will add any positive void
modifier to to-be-hit (eg, AC), but shift any negative void modifier
to to-hit.

This means that the stance which is chosen will be modified no worse
than the character's pre-monkvoid stats, but the stance which is not
chosen will be modified no better.

Monks start aggressive, which means that most monks will start with an
AC of 5 rather than 4, but with no to-hit penalty.  Sacks make a huge
difference to the inventory-management game, so they still have a
one-in-five chance, checked first, to start with one.

